---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base
  title="Method — Gourmet Gastronomer"
  description="How Gourmet Gastronomer treats sources, completeness, and local knowledge."
  permalink="/method/"
  crumbs={[{ name: "Method", url: "/method/" }]}
>
  <main class="home" id="main">
    <p class="eyebrow">Method</p>
    <h1>Method</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Pages are files. Relationships use stable identifiers, not URLs. If a
        file moves, the graph should still hold.
      </p>
      <p>
        We prefer primary sources: universities, extension programs, government
        standards, scientific publications, professional associations, and the
        public sites of producers themselves. We do not invent URLs, quotations,
        addresses, or hours.
      </p>
      <p>
        Incomplete pages are allowed. A sketch is labeled as a sketch. A
        developing article is not dressed up as finished work.
      </p>
      <p>
        We teach observation, not just timers: what the dough, curd, jam, or
        wine is doing, what variables move it, and what failure looks like.
        Safety numbers (canning times, pathogen controls) come from
        authoritative processes. Workshop rules of thumb are labeled as
        practice, not as physics.
      </p>
      <p>
        Atlas entries connect places to knowledge. They are not a business
        directory. We omit hours and telephone numbers because they rot.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
